<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Without this, the system cannot route a CloudKit share link to Flong :
	     it looks the application up in the App Store instead, and a recipient
	     tapping an invitation is told they need a newer version that does not
	     exist. It is what declares that this application accepts a share at
	     all, and `ShareAcceptance` is what it hands the share to. -->
	<key>CKSharingSupported</key>
	<true/>
	<key>BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>com.rslt.Flong.refresh</string>
		<string>com.rslt.Flong.processing</string>
		<string>com.rslt.Flong.continued</string>
		<string>com.rslt.Flong.edition</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Somebody invited to a shared collection who has not accepted yet has
	     no identity for CloudKit to resolve : all the share carries is the
	     address the invitation went to, which draws as a bare telephone
	     number. The reader knows who that is, because it is in their address
	     book. Nothing found there ever leaves the device. -->
	<key>NSContactsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Flong looks up the people you invite to a shared collection, so they show under the name and the face you have for them rather than as a phone number. It stays on this device and is never shared.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Flong fills in the city and country of your profile from where you are. The town is kept, never the coordinate, and it goes nowhere but your own iCloud.</string>
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>fetch</string>
		<string>processing</string>
		<string>remote-notification</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
